#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_length

#% text
# `bit_length(k)` gives the number of bits needed for the integer `k`; for negative `k` it is `bit_length(-k - 1)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_length([0, 1, 255, 256, 1000])
#% output
#= [0, 1, 8, 9, 10]

#% cell
bit_length(-256)
#% output
#= 8

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_length`, `bit_shift_right`, `bit_flip`
